@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "COBOL slice";
}

<h1>COBOL to .NET — this checkout only</h1>
<p>
    This site ports the COBOL members in <code>QCBLSRC</code>.
    RPG, CL, order entry, and the rest of menu <code>SAMMNU</code> stay on IBM i.
</p>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr><th>COBOL object</th><th>.NET equivalent</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>PRO201.CBLLE — Display Providers</td>
            <td><a href="/Providers">/Providers</a> (panel 1 and 2)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>SMPL.CBL COPY DATACPY</td>
            <td>Message: @ViewBag.Copybook</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>VERIFY / VERIFYSQL / VERIFYSQLP</td>
            <td>Arithmetic errors this run: @ViewBag.VerifyErrors (0 is success)</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>
    Option 5 still calls the <code>ART202</code> boundary. That program is RPG and is not rewritten here.
    Provider rows are in-memory sample data; the repository has no PROVIDER data members.
</p>
